Package: trick
Type: Package
Title: Scored Text Find over Conversations and Scientific Catalogues
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hakki", "Sabah", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "hakkisabah@users.noreply.github.com")
    )
Description: A deterministic find with scoring. It splits a conversation into
    sentence-aligned passages, indexes them in memory, and ranks them against a
    query with Okapi BM25, an optional phrase bonus, and an optional external
    probability supplied by the 'laya' decision engine. It also reads and writes
    the fixed-record score matrix used by the companion Python implementation, so
    the same on-disk index serves both languages. No model is embedded and no
    network call is made: every score is computed from data the caller passes in.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
LazyData: false
NeedsCompilation: no
